# eng_text = `due to this migration the people scattered, but there were some who came back to attack the king, they went through 'halflong', 'loomdiñ', ynaukong'(might be nowgong), then they took the elephant as means of transport till they reached ynongkhlaw (which is known as khatsawphra hima (kingdom) in khasi), they settled there and they called us (pnar) "synteng", 'sahteng in khasi (sahteng literally means 'pending').'  
# pbv_text = Tæ ki-paid nei-tæ pra ki pra i-lai, tæ æm wan ki wa uñ dei-dien ya u-uñ kylla chei-ni cha ya u-attack ya u-syiem lai ki na na haflong lai ki dei-loom diñ nei-tæ lai ki naukong tæ dat ki chei-dat ku da u-hati tæ lai ki chadooh che-i-ni cha chei-ni cha nongkhlaw mo, khatsoophra khatsoophra tæ næh noh ki hei-tu manda næh da chong ki he-i-tu nei-tæ i-daw ya i chei-ni ong ki-khynriam i ki-synteng mut wa sahteiñ i, ka-kyntein sahteiñ (sahteng) synteng.
