# sent_id = PakynteinPt07SajarNangliMigration_018
# eng_text = `we could understand that khasi originally are from this place, but we don't call them khasi instead we call them 'khynriam', then in the 'Nawtrep way of saying it, it was 'u khynriam', 'u pnar', 'u bhoi', 'u war', 'u mynri', 'u iynthong', and 'hadem which means u-khynriam nangriam, u-pnar u-lyngkeN, u-bhoi u-khleN, u-hadem u-hasem, u-mynri u-iynthong, u-khyrwang u-ranghang, u-war u-riat.(please cross check i don't know whether the words above really have meanings or its just rhyming). kit u-khynriam nangriam, u-pnar u-lyngkeN, u-bhoi u-khleN, u-hadem u-hasem, u-mynri u-iynthong, u-khyrwang u-ranghang, u-war u-riat..'  
# pbv_text = Tæ nei-tæ u-chim ki ka-ni tæ mut sñiawthooh mut u-khasi ki-ni ki-khasi katni mut ki wa na i nei-ni, hynrei i ym æm u-ong i ki-khasi ong i ki ki-khynriam, i-tæ i-ktein khynriam, i-tæ ong ki i ki-pnar mut kamtæ hynrei ka-ktein hi ong ki ka-ktein ynñiawtræp ong ki-khynriam, u-pnar, u-bhoi, u-war, u-mynri, u-yinthong wa u-hadem tæ mut u-khynriam nangriam, u-pnar u-lyngkeñ, u-bhoi u-khleñ, u-hadem u-hasem, u-mynri u-yinthong, u-khyrwang u-ranghang, u-war u-riat.
